    {
      "id": "cad9f237-69b4-4e5a-95af-842b255feabf",
      "name": "Process Implementation Guide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        48,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 340,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "**Process Implementation Guide**\n\nA fully automated workflow that checks for new job postings every 12 hours and logs the ones it hasn't seen before to a Google Sheet.\n\n**Setup (credentials needed)**\n\n1. **RapidAPI (JSearch)** – Header Auth credential (`X-RapidAPI-Key`), used to search for jobs\n2. **Google Sheets OAuth2** – used to read existing jobs and log new ones\n3. Create the `Jobs` tab using the header row in the sheet note above\n4. Set your Sheet ID in **Get Existing Jobs** and **Log New Job**\n5. Edit **Search Parameters** to match your target role\n6. Activate the workflow once ready"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "dfe9df1f-ab62-4977-b2d7-e4116a519b7f",
      "name": "Google Sheet Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 316,
        "content": "**Google Sheet: Jobs**\n\nCreate a tab named `Jobs` and paste this header row into cell A1 before activating the workflow. Both Google Sheets nodes use these columns.\n\n```\njob_id\ttitle\tcompany\tlocation\turl\tdate_posted\tstatus\n```\n`job_id` is the dedupe key. `status` is left blank for manual tracking."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9981e996-1d59-4829-af95-30cf9bfd8b2a",
      "name": "1. Trigger and Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        416,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 528,
        "content": "**1. Trigger & Config**\n\nRuns every 12 hours and defines the search (title, location, remote flag, date window, excluded keywords) in one Set node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6fdd1cca-4ac8-45c4-be10-558924b0b2b6",
      "name": "2. Fetch and Filter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        960,
        272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "**2. Fetch & Filter Jobs**\n\nCalls the JSearch API on RapidAPI, splits `data.jobs` into one item per job, then drops Senior / Lead / Staff / Principal titles."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4252fe03-c9e5-4566-b7b1-8a8fb5a44560",
      "name": "3. Load Logged Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        976,
        896
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 404,
        "height": 424,
        "content": "**3. Load Logged Jobs**\n\nRuns in parallel with section 2. Reads every row from the `Jobs` sheet so already-seen jobs can be skipped."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "815e88c5-e6db-43ea-9339-04b0b82cba30",
      "name": "4. Dedupe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1632,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 348,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "**4. Dedupe**\n\nCompares fetched jobs (Input A) with sheet rows (Input B) on `job_id`. Only the 'In A only' output continues."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5db3509d-1635-465d-9c9c-69c7133991ea",
      "name": "5. Log New Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2048,
        352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 508,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "**5. Log New Jobs**\n\nAppends each new job to the `Jobs` sheet. `status` stays blank so you can track it manually."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
